<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mukalla</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mukalla is a port city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabian-sea">Arabian Sea</a> coast of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a> and the main seaport of the Hadramawt. In the 18th and 19th centuries it was ruled by the Kasadi family and then by the Qu'aiti sultans, who made it their capital under British protection. It is now the capital of Hadramawt <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/governorate">Governorate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mukalla.jpg" alt="Mukalla" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mohammed Omar Al-Aidaroos · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Khor_al-Mukalla.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
